# Environment variables
#
# Add a real one with a placeholder value here (never a real secret) so
# other developers know it exists. Actual values belong in `.env.local`,
# which .gitignore already excludes from version control.
#
# Next.js only exposes variables prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` to the browser;
# everything else stays server-only:
# https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/configuring/environment-variables
#
# Example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# Monitoring — see docs/MONITORING.md for setup. Every integration below is
# gated on its own variable and safely does nothing when unset, so the app
# runs identically whether or not any of these are configured.

# Sentry error tracking (instrumentation.ts, instrumentation-client.ts).
# A Sentry DSN isn't a secret — it can only be used to send events to your
# project, not read anything — so it's fine to expose to the browser.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0

# Microsoft Clarity session replay/heatmaps (instrumentation-client.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=abcd1234ef

# Vercel Analytics (app/layout.tsx's <Analytics />) needs no variable here —
# it activates automatically once the project is deployed on Vercel with
# Web Analytics turned on, and is a safe no-op everywhere else.
